{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the minimum possible value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{58 - 42x} + \\sqrt{149 - 140 \\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\), we will analyze the behavior of each term and the overall expression.\n\nFirst, let's denote the expression by \\(f(x) = \\sqrt{58 - 42x} + \\sqrt{149 - 140 \\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\).\n\nWe need to determine the domain of \\(x\\). Since \\(x\\) is in the interval \\([-1, 1]\\), we need to ensure that the expressions under the square roots are non-negative.\n\nFor the first term, \\(\\sqrt{58 - 42x}\\), the expression inside the square root must be non-negative:\n\\[58 - 42x \\geq 0 \\implies x \\leq \\frac{58}{42} = \\frac{29}{21} \\approx 1.38.\\]\nSince \\(x\\) is in \\([-1, 1]\\), this condition is always satisfied.\n\nFor the second term, \\(\\sqrt{149 - 140 \\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\), the expression inside the square root must be non-negative:\n\\[149 - 140 \\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\geq 0 \\implies 149 \\geq 140 \\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\implies \\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\leq \\frac{149}{140} \\approx 1.064.\\]\nSince \\(\\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\leq 1\\) for all \\(x \\in [-1, 1]\\), this condition is always satisfied.\n\n","prefix_end":1043,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,8028,3204,897,315,279,7493,1124,11520,26888,90,20,23,481,220,19,17,87,92,488,1124,26888,90,16,19,24,481,220,16,19,15,1124,26888,90,16,481,856,61,17,3417,59,701,582,686,23643,279,7709,315,1817,4647,323,279,8084,7493,382,5338,11,1077,594,78064,279,7493,553,17767,69,2075,8,284,1124,26888,90,20,23,481,220,19,17,87,92,488,1124,26888,90,16,19,24,481,220,16,19,15,1124,26888,90,16,481,856,61,17,3417,59,3593,1654,1184,311,8253,279,7947,315,17767,87,59,568,8704,17767,87,57758,374,304,279,9873,1124,41197,16,11,220,16,17960,701,582,1184,311,5978,429,279,23393,1212,279,9334,19703,525,2477,60935,382,2461,279,1156,4647,11,1124,11520,26888,90,20,23,481,220,19,17,87,11035,